# PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER

PROJECT_DESCRIPTION_PLACEHOLDER

## Getting started

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) and,
optionally, [just](https://github.com/casey/just).

```bash
git clone https://github.com/OWNER_PLACEHOLDER/PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER
cd PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER

uv sync              # creates .venv from uv.lock, installs dev tools too
just check           # format + lint + types + tests: the whole gate
```

`uv sync` pins the interpreter from `.python-version` and installs it if it is
missing - you do not need a system Python of that version.

You never have to activate the virtualenv: `uv run <cmd>` uses it. If you
prefer an activated shell, `source .venv/bin/activate`, or install
[direnv](https://direnv.net/) and run `direnv allow` to pick up `.envrc`.

