## Use it

```bash
uv run PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER --help
uv run PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER hello --name ada --times 2
uv run PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER info          # resolved config as JSON
```

## Install it

No PyPI release needed - install straight from git:

```bash
uv tool install git+https://github.com/OWNER_PLACEHOLDER/PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER@v0.1.0
PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER --help
```

Or run it once without installing:

```bash
uvx --from git+https://github.com/OWNER_PLACEHOLDER/PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER --help
```

### Shell completion

Built into tyro. Nothing else to install:

```bash
# zsh
mkdir -p ~/.zfunc
PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER --tyro-write-completion zsh ~/.zfunc/_PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER
# then in ~/.zshrc:  fpath+=~/.zfunc && autoload -Uz compinit && compinit

# bash
dir="${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/bash-completion/completions"
mkdir -p "$dir"
PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER --tyro-write-completion bash "$dir/PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER"
```

## Configuration

Every setting has a default, can be overridden in `.env`, and can be overridden
again by an environment variable prefixed `ENV_PREFIX_PLACEHOLDER`. Copy
`.env.example` to `.env` to start. `PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER info` prints what
the program actually resolved.
